From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:44:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: use high-speed SD during bring-up

SDR104 repeatedly loses the attached SD16G card during log writes, with
command timeouts and failed recovery. Keep the external slot at SD High
Speed and avoid the 1.8 V UHS transition until that path is diagnosed.
This deliberately limits performance rather than claiming UHS support.

On SM-T531, the resulting 50 MHz, 4-bit, 3.3 V mode passed 8 MiB write,
sync, unmount, cache-drop and readback-hash checks on both ext2 boot and
ext4 Debian partitions. MMC timeout and CRC counters remained zero.
Later writes still caused CMD13 timeouts and card re-enumeration. This
limit is a diagnostic baseline, not a storage reliability fix. The internal
eMMC configuration is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -103,3 +103,9 @@
 	vddio-supply = <&pm8226_l5>;
 	vddiol8-supply = <&pm8226_l8>;
 };
+
+&sdhc_2 {
+	/* SDR104 currently fails sustained card I/O during bring-up. */
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
+	no-1-8-v;
+};
-- 
